Backport of upstream 3960ac04 ("misc: avoid saving some heap garbage", notaz,
2025-12-27) to the pinned revisions that predate it. SaveState mallocs the GPU
freeze block and gpulib fills only ulControl[0..15] and [0xe0..0xe7], so the
rest of ulControl carried whatever the heap held: two devices in identical
emulated state produced different save states, and every hash-based netplay
check (Netplay's and RetroArch's CRC) saw a desync that was not there
(Crash Team Racing, spruce RG35XXH and Brick, 2026-11-05).

diff --git a/libpcsxcore/misc.c b/libpcsxcore/misc.c
--- a/libpcsxcore/misc.c
+++ b/libpcsxcore/misc.c
@@ -767,6 +767,7 @@ int SaveState(const char *file) {
 	gpufP = (GPUFreeze_t *)malloc(sizeof(GPUFreeze_t));
 	if (gpufP == NULL) goto cleanup;
 	gpufP->ulFreezeVersion = 1;
+	memset(gpufP->ulControl, 0, sizeof(gpufP->ulControl));
 	GPU_freeze(1, gpufP);
 	SaveFuncs.write(f, gpufP, sizeof(GPUFreeze_t));
 	free(gpufP); gpufP = NULL;
